{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>It is not good that the man should be alone.</b> The good of the intended end — that he be in His likeness and image — will not be attained if he must himself engage in the needs of his livelihood." "<b>A help meet for him.</b> A help who will be equal to him in image and likeness, for this is necessary to him in knowing his needs and providing for them at the proper time. And he said כנגדו (\"as against him\") because when something is placed on a balance-pan opposite another thing, if they are equal in weight, they stand opposite each other in a straight line; but when the two weighed things are not equal, one rises and the other falls, and they do not stand opposite each other in a straight line. In this manner our Sages, of blessed memory, said: Moses was weighed against all Israel (Mekhilta, Yitro 1). However, it was not fitting that the helper be entirely equal to him, for then it would not be fitting that one of them serve and minister to the other."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:28:43.088687206Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}